{"index":111,"pointer":"/findings/4/acceptance_criteria","value":{"static":["Limit WP66-A §8 pure-display/no-side-effect guarantees so they inherit existing dynamic-read and cache behavior; reference existing R4-IF rather than recreate its rules.","Correct WP28 bottle final-state contract with the above ordered normal party chain, including first0/empty-time, fresh-time/reuse, KeyItem inventory and observation after final refresh.","Supply a bounded static first-use vector and fresh-time/no-middle-read contrasts; distinguish handler return from bag-session return and original request from current stored state.","Keep all ordinary menu/data/media premises and timing-window qualification; do not change R4-IF, primary same-value rules or introduce rollback."],"optional":["WP21 may add a short cross-reference/example explaining callback reentry and the original requested-form parameter; the existing primitive order/same-value rule is already correct, so a separate mandatory rewrite is unnecessary."],"no_required_revision":["WP18/WP21/WP15 existing display-read rules, R4-IF01–06 and existing equal-value explicit submission rules.","Existing SPINDA pixel, hatching and form-handler learning-cancellation rules are not reopened."],"must_execute":[]}}
